Card roles








Card
Cost
Role




Omnipresence
{5}{G}{G}{G}
Engine keystone: spells with mana value at or below your creature count cost nothing from hand. Three copies, and Pia tutors for it


Face Yourself
{5}{R}{R}
Primary payoff: a hasty token copy of every creature you control, which is a lethal swing the turn it resolves; the copies survive the end step if you control a planeswalker


Verdant Kraken
{4}{G}{G}{G}
Engine and payoff: a 3/3 Forest Tentacle land creature token at the beginning of each player’s upkeep, so the count grows twice per round and each token taps for {G}


Emrakul, the Exigent Doom
{10}
Second win: 12/12 flying trample with ward, untaps all lands when cast, and can be exiled from hand for {3} to turn a land into a {T}: Add {C}{C} source


Ghalta the Unstoppable
{8}{G}
Cost-reduced 8/8 trampler that grants the whole team trample; free off Omnipresence at nine creatures


Garruk, Curse Breaker
{3}{G}{G}
Mana and bodies: +2 untaps two lands, -3 makes a 4/4 Beast, and his static draws a card whenever a creature with power 4 or greater enters. Also the planeswalker that keeps Face Yourself’s copies alive


Loot, the Nexus
{2}{G}
Mana engine: taps for one mana of any colour per distinct power among your creatures


Simulacrum Shaper
{1}{G}{G}
Two-drop ramp that replaces itself when it dies


Greenhouse Propagator
{2}{G}
{G} source plus a life on every creature entry, which sizes Germinate Recruits


Pia, Aether Ascetic
{2}{G}
Enchantment tutor: discard a card, find Omnipresence


Jiang Yanggu, Never Alone
{3}{G}
Two bodies in one card (Mowu is a 3/3, a third distinct power for Loot) and untaps all tokens at end of turn


Hexhaven Invigorator
{G}{G}{G}{G}
6/6 vigilance wall whose damage trigger fetches that many lands tapped; also a 6-power body for Loot


Germinate Recruits
{2}{W}
Instant-speed Cadet burst sized by life gained this turn; the cleanest way to jump from three creatures to six

Card roles








Card
Cost
Role in the engine




Emberheart Challenger
{1}{R}
Valiant payoff: targeting him exiles the top card and lets you play it this turn


Whiskerquill Scribe
{1}{R}
Valiant payoff and the cheapest discard outlet for Monument


Flowerfoot Swordmaster
{W}
One-mana Valiant body; targeting her pumps every Mouse you control


Seedglaive Mentor
{1}{R}{W}
Valiant payoff that grows permanently, on a 3/2 vigilance haste body


Red Room Recruit
{1}{B}
Villain that connives on entry; a legal Villainous Hideout target


Mob Lookout
{1}{U/B}
Points a connive at any creature you control, so it also fires Valiant


Magda, the Hoardmaster
{1}{R}
Primary win: three Treasures become a 4/4 flying haste Scorpion Dragon, once a turn


Reckless Lackey
{R}
One-mana first strike attacker that later trades for a card and a Treasure


Charming Scoundrel
{1}{R}
Modal two-drop: a Treasure, a loot, or a Wicked Role on a Valiant creature


Gold Rush
{1}{G}
Signature enabler: a Treasure plus +2/+2 per Treasure on a targeted creature


Ancestors’ Aid
{1}{R}
Treasure plus first strike; a combat trick that is also an engine piece


Reckless Ransacking
{1}{R}
Treasure plus +3/+2, to win a blocked attack


Unstable Experiment
{1}{U}
Instant-speed connive, a card for you or a crime against an opponent


Monument to Endurance
{3}
Discard payoff: draw, Treasure, or each opponent loses 3 life


Collector’s Vault
{2}
Repeatable loot and Treasure every turn, and a Monument trigger

Card roles








Card
Cost
Role




Denzilore Fatehold
{1}{W}{U}{U}
Primary engine and primary threat: flash 3/4 flier, +1/+1 on each creature per surveil


Yoshimaru, Beloved Companion
{2}{W}
Counter doubler: turns Denzilore’s trigger into +2/+2 team-wide, and Hydra’s placement into two counters


Proctor of Potential
{W}{U}
Repeatable surveil trigger on a 3/1 body; recurs itself from the graveyard for {W}{U}


Surveillance Phantasm
{1}{U}
Evasive counter carrier (flying, vigilance); attacks only after a surveil, which is free with Eye of Jace


Guiding Hydra
{X}{W}
Counter distributor: one counter becomes one on every other creature at combat, doubled by Yoshimaru


Graft Surgeon
{2}{W}
Insurance: its counter moves to a flier when it dies, keeping the pump on the board


Darklight Phoenix
{3}{B}
Recursive threat and graveyard payoff: returns from the graveyard after a two-creature turn


Eye of Jace
{1}
Turn-one surveil engine; converts a seven-card graveyard into two damage to each opponent


Prophesied End
{1}{W}
Two-mana unconditional removal; the card draw it gives is a real cost, so aim it at attackers or at the creature you must kill


Refute Destiny
{1}{W}
Exile removal for green and blue creatures and planeswalkers, with surveil 1 attached


Generous Revival
{2}{W}
Recursion for a cheap engine piece with a +1/+1 counter; flashback {4}{W} from the graveyard


Cast Away Doubt
{2}{B}
Two cards and two damage to each player; the life loss is paid by the opponent too

