Card
Cost
Role in the engine




Sanctum Lurker
{2}{B}
The loophole: zero-loyalty planeswalkers survive, and every planeswalker gains the ping ability


Mindseeker Oculus
{2}{U}
Three mana for four loyalty, the best rate in the deck


Keeper of the Quiet Hour
{3}
Colorless body that empowers two, fixes the curve for any mana base


Way of the Pyromancer
{1}{R}
Two loyalty on entry, then every planeswalker has “[+1]: Add {R}”


Way of the Deathbringer
{2}{B}
Five loyalty on entry, every planeswalker can eat a creature for a 4/4 Beast


Way of the Warlord
{2}{R}
Five loyalty on entry, every planeswalker can deal 2 to a creature and 2 to a player


Jace’s Machinations
{2}{U}
Eight loyalty at instant speed, and loyalty abilities become instant-speed that turn


Violent Echoes
{2}{R}{R}
Six damage removal that converts excess damage into loyalty


No Admittance
{1}{R}
Three damage to anything, plus one loyalty


Solve for Disappointment
{1}{B}
Discard plus one loyalty, the cheapest way to start the token count


Plan for All Outcomes
{3}{U}
Repeatable empower one every turn you cast a noncreature spell


The Theorist, Jace Beleren
{2}{U}{U}
Draws on every opponent draw step, makes Illusions to feed Deathbringer


Chandra, Torch of Defiance
{2}{R}{R}
Removal, ramp, and a seven-loyalty emblem as a third finisher


Ajani Unrelenting
{4}{R}{R}
Every loyalty activation makes a 2/2 Cadet; the plus one gives the team haste


Massacre Girl, Most Wanted
{4}{B}
Grows a +1/+1 counter from every point of noncombat damage the ping engine deals


Overwrite the Multiverse
{4}{B}{B}
Reset button that pays out one loyalty per creature exiled

Card roles








Card
Cost
Role




Sanctum Lurker
{2}{B}
Engine keystone, 3/2: planeswalkers survive at 0 loyalty, and every planeswalker gains “[+2]: 1 damage to each opponent and you gain 1 life”


Way of the Deathbringer
{2}{B}
Primary payoff: gives every planeswalker “[-2]: sacrifice a creature, create a 4/4 green Beast with trample”; empower Jace 5 on entry


Way of the Necromancer
{1}{B}
Sacrifice refund: every creature death puts a loyalty counter on each planeswalker, so the Beast forge re-arms itself; empower Jace 2 on entry


Way of the Mentor
{2}{W}
Second refund engine: every life gain (including Lurker’s drain) adds a loyalty counter to every planeswalker; empower Jace 5 on entry


Way of the Pyromancer
{1}{R}
Mana engine: every planeswalker gains “[+1]: Add {R}”, which pays for the deck’s red half; empower Jace 2 on entry


Command the Stage
{2}{R}
Fodder engine: a Cadet plus a +1/+1 counter on each other Wizard token, and it returns from the graveyard at each upkeep whenever an opponent took noncombat damage


Repurposed Enforcer
{1}{W}
Two-mana 3/2 that empowers on attack for X equal to your creature count, which is the deck’s biggest single empower


Screeching Soulbreaker
{2}{B}
1/4 flier that drains 1 from each opponent on attack; that is noncombat damage, so it also rebuys Command the Stage


Mabel, Valley Hero
{1}{R}{W}
Counter distributor on a 1/2: every creature that enters, including every Cadet, can be given a +1/+1 counter


Edgar, Ancient Bloodlord
{W}{B}
Two-mana 2/3 that gains a life on every creature or planeswalker death and converts spare bodies into +1/+1 counters and menace


Stingerquill Charm
{B}{R}
Modal instant: 3 damage, first strike plus deathtouch, or a hasty Cadet for the Beast forge


No Admittance
{1}{R}
Two-mana 3 damage to any target that also empowers Jace 1, so the removal spell builds the engine it is protecting

