Cost
Role in the engine




Guardian Sunmare
{3}{W}{W}
The engine: free permanent with mana value 3 or less on every saddled attack, which discounts power-up


Stubborn Burrowfiend
{1}{G}
Mill on saddle, then grows with the graveyard it fills


Ornery Tumblewagg
{2}{G}
Combat counter, then doubles counters when saddled, the deck’s clock


White Tiger, Ava Ayala
{1}{G}
Chevron target for Sunmare, power-up makes a 4/4 The Tiger God


Seraphic Steed
{G}{W}
Two-drop body that makes a 3/3 Angel token on every saddled attack, tokens pay future saddle costs


Bold Biochemist
{1}{U}
Sunmare target, power-up draws two cards for four mana after entering


Blossoming Tortoise
{2}{G}{G}
Mills three on entry and attack, returns a land, and makes land abilities cost one less


Hedge Shredder
{2}{G}{G}
Crew 1 attacker that mills two and puts milled lands onto the battlefield tapped


Alacrian Armory
{3}{W}
Saddles a Mount at the beginning of combat for free, plus vigilance and +0/+1 to the team


Guidelight Matrix
{2}
Cantrips on entry, then saddles a Mount for {2} without tapping a single creature


Riverchurn Monument
{1}{U}
Repeatable opponent mill, then an exhaust that doubles their graveyard


The Water Crystal
{2}{U}{U}
Adds four cards to every opposing mill, turns two Monuments into a kill


Dark Matter Manipulator
{B}
One-drop that mills three and scales off graveyard size


Unliving Legionnaire
{3}{B}
Flying body whose power-up returns a creature from the graveyard to hand


Run Over
{1}{G}
One-mana fight when it targets your Mount, the deck’s main removal
